1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,106
Buying a used car means trusting photos and paperwork you can't verify.

2
00:00:04,106 --> 00:00:08,849
Veriqo shows the buyer what the photos reveal, what the record says, what is still

3
00:00:08,849 --> 00:00:11,452
uncertain, and what to inspect before paying.

4
00:00:12,057 --> 00:00:13,305
Here's how it works.

5
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:17,797
The buyer adds photos, the registration number and the seller's listing.

6
00:00:17,797 --> 00:00:22,289
Gemini 2.5 Flash on Vertex AI turns the photos into structured findings.

7
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:26,906
A registration lookup adds record facts, which are simulated in this demo.

8
00:00:26,906 --> 00:00:32,333
Then a deterministic rules engine scores everything, and the report labels each finding

9
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:35,203
as observed, record, inferred, or not checked.

10
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:37,524
Now the live app on Cloud Run.

11
00:00:37,524 --> 00:00:42,571
I enter a synthetic test plate and the make and model from the listing, then upload five

12
00:00:42,571 --> 00:00:44,177
openly licensed test photos.

13
00:00:44,177 --> 00:00:47,733
Each photo is numbered, so every finding can point back to it.

14
00:00:48,335 --> 00:00:52,615
Gemini is analysing the photos now, and this wait is real, not edited.

15
00:00:52,615 --> 00:00:55,611
Each photo is sent with a strict response schema:

16
00:00:55,611 --> 00:01:00,747
the defect, where it is, its severity on a fixed rubric, which photo shows it, which

17
00:01:00,747 --> 00:01:03,987
views of the car are covered, and a confidence score.

18
00:01:03,987 --> 00:01:07,961
The temperature is zero, so the same photos give the same answer.

19
00:01:08,564 --> 00:01:09,633
Here is the result.

20
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,039
The score is not a guess.

21
00:01:11,039 --> 00:01:15,765
It is the sum of published points for each finding, and this bar shows how much came

22
00:01:15,765 --> 00:01:18,916
from the visible condition, the record, and uncertainty.

23
00:01:19,518 --> 00:01:21,837
Each finding carries one of four labels.

24
00:01:21,837 --> 00:01:26,824
Observed means Gemini saw it in a photo, shown right beside it, like the worn tyre and

25
00:01:26,824 --> 00:01:27,636
the torn seat.

26
00:01:27,636 --> 00:01:32,100
Record means it was read from the registration data, such as the active loan.

27
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:36,449
Inferred means a rule was applied to that data, like the expired insurance.

28
00:01:36,449 --> 00:01:41,668
And not checked lists what photos can never prove, such as accident history or the engine.

29
00:01:42,267 --> 00:01:47,529
Because this registration record is synthetic test data, it is labelled simulated, not

30
00:01:47,529 --> 00:01:50,038
government verified, wherever it appears.

31
00:01:50,639 --> 00:01:54,506
The buyer then gets a prioritised checklist of what to do before paying.

32
00:01:55,107 --> 00:01:59,668
The report is saved in Firestore, with the photos in a private Cloud Storage bucket.

33
00:01:59,668 --> 00:02:04,337
Reloading the link restores it, and the audit trail shows every step that produced it.

34
00:02:04,938 --> 00:02:06,095
Now a failure case:

35
00:02:06,095 --> 00:02:08,957
a blurry photo, and a plate that has no record.

36
00:02:08,957 --> 00:02:11,514
Watch what Veriqo does with weak evidence.

37
00:02:12,114 --> 00:02:17,405
It lowers its confidence, makes no claims it cannot see, and marks the registration as

38
00:02:17,405 --> 00:02:19,866
not verified, instead of inventing data.

39
00:02:20,468 --> 00:02:21,480
Under the hood:

40
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:26,200
Cloud Run, Gemini 2.5 Flash on Vertex AI, Firestore and Cloud Storage.

41
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:31,932
We tested it with automated API tests, scoring rule checks, and browser tests on this

42
00:02:31,932 --> 00:02:36,113
live deployment, and fixed the model errors those tests found.

43
00:02:36,113 --> 00:02:36,585
Veriqo.

44
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:38,877
Know what to check before you buy.
